        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "# ASSIGNMENT_QUEUE.md\n\nWe will need 5 iterations.\n\n1. **Define Core SAT Variables**  \n   Establish the essential state variables and constants required for the solver baseline.  \n   Output: `ASSIGNMENT_01.md`\n\n2. **Constraint Encoding Schema**  \n   Specify the method for encoding logical constraints into the SAT system, including supported operators.  \n   Output: `ASSIGNMENT_02.md`\n\n3. **Iterator Workflow Definition**  \n   Detail how iteration progresses (input, processing, output), including fail-safes and checkpoints.  \n   Output: `ASSIGNMENT_03.md`\n\n4. **Overseer-Iterator Interface**  \n   Define the minimal interface rules for communication between Overseer and Iterator modules.  \n   Output: `ASSIGNMENT_04.md`\n\n5. **Reporting & Integration Checks**  \n   Specify reporting hooks, integration checks with `sat_core_report.py`, and acceptance outputs.  \n   Output: `ASSIGNMENT_05.md`\n\n**Parallelization guidance:**  \n- Tasks 1 and 2 can run in parallel (Wave 1).  \n- Task 3 requires Task 1.  \n- Task 4 requires Task 3.  \n- Task 5 requires all prior tasks (final wave).  \n\n**Integrator Sentinel rule:**  \nIf k > N: “No such assignment exists, therefore I am the Integrator. Please upload the outputs of the previous N iterations.”  \n\nHALT"
          ]
        },
